Pi-DOS: Preserve overlapping FPU register views under strict aliasing.

RegBit specializations all access the same underlying control/status word.
GCC 14 on AArch64 can otherwise cache one specialization's data across a
write through another. In FPTAN, clearing C2 after pushing 1.0 restores the
old TOP bits, leaving the guest with an incorrect x87 stack. FSINCOS has
the same ordering. This corrupts trig tables in Wolfenstein 3D with both
the normal and dynrec cores.

Mark the register views as aliasing types instead of changing instruction
semantics or disabling strict aliasing for the entire emulator.

--- a/include/fpu.h
+++ b/include/fpu.h
@@ -328,7 +328,9 @@
 };
 
 template<class T, unsigned bitno, unsigned nbits=1>
-struct RegBit
+// Different specializations are overlapping views of the same register.
+// A write through one view must invalidate cached data in every other view.
+struct GCC_ATTRIBUTE(may_alias) RegBit
 {
 	enum { basemask = (1 << nbits) - 1 };
 	enum { mask = basemask << bitno };
